{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c471","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b051-fe1f-7003-b3e2-8d6f1f519698"},"sequence":147,"recorded_at":1780531400000289,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b052-7311-7420-8dc9-1593b6a70e07"},"task_id":"01a0b052-7311-7420-8dc9-1593b6a70e07","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b052-7311-7420-8dc9-1593b6a70e07","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-5-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-219okr) { checklist outcomeResources notes }' 2>&1 | head -n 120\",\n  \"description\": \"Read task checklist and resources\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Negotiate supported majors, preserve core-only peers, expose unsupported directory/backend activation, and refuse no-common-major\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft \\\\u003ccheckpoint_oid\\\\u003e` before completing again.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":true}],\\\"notes\\\":\\\"TASK-260908-2tkufa assigns the approved v0.6.0 delta owner. Original AC and partial work remain preserved; pending runtime support is not claimed by catalog adoption. Own subsequent major negotiation under sections 11.2-11.3/17 with adopted RPC 5 and explicit historical RPC 2/3/4 bounds. Config-4 Host Channel endpoints select RPC 5 only; legacy installations keep explicit historical behavior. Negotiation cannot downgrade a required authenticated endpoint or substitute for TASK-260830-z1yxg9 admission.\\\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/max pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:009eecf230ad676c71fa02f210ad171dc6936cae601b3bc028fa753d219ff3c1 rationale=\\\\\\\"Next fan-out (M2 first leaf: RPC major negotiation over rpcwire/hostchannel) unblocked by STORY-260830-1kiyj6; muse-spark max is the primary configured producer.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260917-b15a5b, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260917-b15a5b)\\\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (muse) (exit=0)\\\\nspawn run completed: muse (run=RUN-260917-b15a5b, pid=76784, exit=0)\\\\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260917-b15a5b queued successor RUN-260917-244f06 (attempt 1/3, model=muse-spark): Change Request construction for TASK-260830-219okr failed: Change Request CR-TASK-260830-219okr-1 revision 1 validation failed at command 5/27 (1-based) with exit code 1; log resource TASK-260830-219okr_change-request_rev1-validation.log; retry: fix the failure and complete the producer again; the configured suite will rerun automatically\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260917-244f06)\\\",\\\"outcomeResources\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260917-b15a5b.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260917-b15a5b.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"System spawn log captured by task-board\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_results.md\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_results.md\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Handoff evidence: results and AC coverage\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"AC conformance matrix with call sites and mutants\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_producer-evidence.tar.gz\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_producer-evidence.tar.gz\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Producer evidence archive: logs, mutant per-plant runs, validation\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_change-request_rev1.patch\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_change-request_rev1.patch\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Change Request CR-TASK-260830-219okr-1 revision 1 candidate patch (repository_delta=present, 8 changed paths)\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_change-request_rev1-validation.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_change-request_rev1-validation.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Change Request CR-TASK-260830-219okr-1 revision 1 bounded validation log\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260917-244f06.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260917-244f06.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"System spawn log captured by task-board\\\"}]}\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6024,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1506,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c473","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b051-fe1f-7003-b3e2-8d6f1f519698"},"sequence":148,"recorded_at":1780531400000291,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b052-7311-7420-8dc9-1593b6a70e07"},"task_id":"01a0b052-7311-7420-8dc9-1593b6a70e07","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b052-7311-7420-8dc9-1593b6a70e07"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c475","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b051-fe1f-7003-b3e2-8d6f1f519698"},"sequence":149,"recorded_at":1780531400000293,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0526a477371b05729f7c1b897a1","text":"<read-skill-result name=\"bundled:durable-test-collateral\" status=\"ok\">\n<metadata>\npath: /Users/iv/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core/skills/durable-test-collateral/SKILL.md\nlocator: file:///Users/iv/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core/skills/durable-test-collateral/SKILL.md\nsource: bundled\nbytes_returned: 2748\nbytes_total: 2748\ntruncated: false\n</metadata>\n\nRelative paths in a skill body resolve against that skill's directory (the `skill-dir` value on its wrapper, or the parent of SKILL.md); use absolute paths in tool calls.\n\n<skill-body id=\"bundled:durable-test-collateral\" skill-dir=\"/Users/iv/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core/skills/durable-test-collateral\">\n---\nname: durable-test-collateral\ndescription: Load the body before the first implementation edit for a bug fix or behavior change, or when the user or governing specification makes reusable tests a deliverable. It keeps the smallest focused test with the delivered project and updates coverage when behavior changes. Do not load for greenfield work unless reusable tests are explicitly required, behavior-preserving refactors, verification-only work, plan/review/explanation/documentation/formatting/generated-output-only work, explicit no-change or no-tool work, or when the user declines tests.\nuser-invocable: false\n---\n\n# Durable Test Collateral\n\nVerification is part of the delivered project when it can prevent the same\nbehavior from breaking again. Use the project&apos;s existing framework and\nconventions.\n\n## Keep the check with the project\n\nFor a bug fix or behavior change, add or update the smallest maintained test in\nthe repository&apos;s normal test layout that exercises the changed behavior. If a\nspecification makes a reusable suite or test category a deliverable, implement\nthat suite instead of treating it as private verification.\n\nAn inline interpreter command, heredoc, scratch script, temporary-directory\ntest, demo, or manual probe may help diagnose the problem, but it does not\nreplace the maintained test. Keep a useful self-authored test unless the user\nexplicitly asks for a disposable probe.\n\nDo not add a new test framework solely to satisfy this skill. If the repository\nhas no maintained harness and the request does not require one, disclose when\ndurable coverage would be disproportionate or infeasible and use the narrowest\nhonest verification instead.\n\nOn a later turn, update the maintained test even when the old suite remains\ngreen and the user does not repeat the test request. Cover the new behavior,\nnot merely an unrelated cleanup in the test file.\n\n## Prove the maintained check\n\nObserve the authentic failure before the implementation change when it is safe\nand runnable. Then make the smallest implementation change and run the focused\nmaintained test after the final relevant source or test edit.\n\nDo not weaken or delete a real failing test to obtain green. Fix the product,\nor explain why the test&apos;s expectation is wrong before changing that\nexpectation. Do not repeat an unchanged check solely to collect evidence.\n\nRun a broad or full suite only when the user, a repository gate, or\nproportionate risk requires it. A focused regression test comes first; broad\nproof does not substitute for missing focused coverage.\n\nIf the real runner is unavailable but the focused test can still be authored\nhonestly, leave the focused test in the repository and say it was not run. Do\nnot fabricate a passing result.\n\n</skill-body>\n</read-skill-result>","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_skill","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c477","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b051-fe1f-7003-b3e2-8d6f1f519698"},"sequence":150,"recorded_at":1780531400000295,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0526ba274a1a46f22da9f41aa88","text":"Read text file `internal/meshneg/negotiate.go`.\n1|// Package meshneg selects the single Mesh RPC major spoken on one peer\n2|// connection from the local installation's configuration generation and the\n3|// peer's decoded hello. It frames nothing, opens no connection, performs no\n4|// I/O, keeps no state, and admits no peer: identity equality, allowlist\n5|// membership, and trust generation remain the hostchannel admission boundary\n6|// (TASK-260830-z1yxg9), which negotiation never substitutes.\n7|//\n8|// The package owns the Section 11.2-11.3/11.8/11.9/11.10.1 and Section 17\n9|// selection rules only: highest common major among the locally offered and\n10|// peer offered majors, core-only preservation with explicit unsupported\n11|// directory/backend activation exposure, and no-common-major refusal with the\n12|// pinned Section 15 class. Wire shapes (hello maps, namespaces, operation\n13|// registry), Structured Error bindings, and configuration parsing stay with\n14|// their landed owners (rpcwire, axerror, config); this package derives from\n15|// them and never restates them.\n16|package meshneg\n17|\n18|import (\n19|\t\"errors\"\n20|\t\"fmt\"\n21|\t\"regexp\"\n22|\t\"slices\"\n23|\t\"strconv\"\n24|\t\"strings\"\n25|\n26|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n27|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/rpcwire\"\n28|)\n29|\n30|// Pinned RPC framing versions this negotiator can select. A frame carrying\n31|// any other version is not a lower minor of a supported major; Sections\n32|// 11.2-11.10 pin exactly these four, and Section 17.2 rule 1 requires a\n33|// reader to reject an unsupported major rather than coerce it.\n34|var pinnedFrameVersions = map[string]int{\n35|\t\"2.0.0\": 2,\n36|\t\"3.0.0\": 3,\n37|\t\"4.0.0\": 4,\n38|\t\"5.0.0\": 5,\n39|}\n40|\n41|// directoryFeatureMajor is the first RPC major that negotiates directory\n42|// replication (Section 11.8). backendEvidenceFeatureMajor is the first RPC\n43|// major that negotiates TerminalBackend evidence replication (Section 11.9);\n44|// RPC 5 retains the exact RPC-4 shapes (Section 11.10.1).\n45|const (\n46|\tdirectoryFeatureMajor       = 3\n47|\tbackendEvidenceFeatureMajor = 4\n48|)\n49|\n50|// Exposure codes for above-core activation on a negotiated peer. Both are\n51|// registered Section 15.3 codes; neither is minted here.\n52|const (\n53|\t// DirectoryUnsupportedCode is the literal Section 11.8 exposure token:\n54|\t// a node negotiating core-only with a peer reports that peer as\n55|\t// directory_mesh_unsupported, never as zero inventory.\n56|\tDirectoryUnsupportedCode = axerror.Code(\"directory_mesh_unsupported\")\n57|\t// BackendEvidenceUnsupportedCode is the RPC-4 equivalent: Section 11.9\n58|\t// requires reporting TerminalBackend evidence unsupported rather than\n59|\t// empty, and Section 17.4 requires reporting activation unavailable\n60|\t// rather than omitting the session. terminal_backend_unavailable is\n61|\t// the registered exit-6 code that states exactly that.\n62|\tBackendEvidenceUnsupportedCode = axerror.Code(\"terminal_backend_unavailable\")\n63|)\n64|\n65|// RefusalReason names why negotiation selected no major. Automation branches\n66|// on Reason (and Code); Detail is human text only.\n67|type RefusalReason string\n68|\n69|const (\n70|\t// ReasonUnknownConfig reports a local configuration generation outside\n71|\t// 1.0.0-4.0.0. Section 6.6 refuses unknown configuration instead of\n72|\t// selecting legacy.\n73|\tReasonUnknownConfig RefusalReason = \"unknown_config\"\n74|\t// ReasonUnsupportedFrame reports a peer frame version outside the\n75|\t// pinned 2.0.0-5.0.0 vocabulary.\n76|\tReasonUnsupportedFrame RefusalReason = \"unsupported_frame\"\n77|\t// ReasonContractShape reports a peer hello whose contracts map is not\n78|\t// exactly the framing major's pinned profile (missing, extra, or\n79|\t// extension keys, or a wrong rpc array shape).\n80|\tReasonContractShape RefusalReason = \"contract_shape\"\n81|\t// ReasonMixedMajor reports a peer rpc offer that mixes majors or\n82|\t// disagrees with its framing major. Section 17.1 forbids selecting a\n83|\t// major by coercion.\n84|\tReasonMixedMajor RefusalReason = \"mixed_major\"\n85|\t// ReasonNoCommonMajor reports disjoint local and peer major sets.\n86|\tReasonNoCommonMajor RefusalReason = \"no_common_major\"\n87|)\n88|\n89|var (\n90|\t// ErrUnknownConfig is the cause of an unknown-configuration refusal.\n91|\tErrUnknownConfig = errors.New(\"unknown configuration generation\")\n92|\t// ErrUnsupportedFrame is the cause of an unsupported-frame refusal.\n93|\tErrUnsupportedFrame = errors.New(\"unsupported RPC frame version\")\n94|\t// ErrContractShape is the cause of a contract-shape refusal.\n95|\tErrContractShape = errors.New(\"hello contracts differ from the pinned profile\")\n96|\t// ErrMixedMajor is the cause of a mixed-major refusal.\n97|\tErrMixedMajor = errors.New(\"peer rpc offer mixes majors\")\n98|\t// ErrNoCommonMajor is the cause of a no-common-major refusal.\n99|\tErrNoCommonMajor = errors.New(\"no common RPC major\")\n100|)\n101|\n102|// Refusal is the pure-data no-selection outcome. It frames no wire bytes:\n103|// Sections 11.2 and 15.1 close without a peer error frame on an unsupported\n104|// major, and Section 11.10.1 closes without a frame on other RPC majors, so\n105|// the only peer-visible effect is the close itself. The initiator maps Code\n106|// and ExitCode to its own local Structured Error; this value is that mapping\n107|// input, never a forged peer response.\n108|type Refusal struct {\n109|\t// Code and ExitCode are the pinned Section 15 class, resolved from the\n110|\t// axerror registry rather than retyped.\n111|\tCode     axerror.Code\n112|\tExitCode int\n113|\t// Reason names the refusal shape; Detail is human text.\n114|\tReason RefusalReason\n115|\tDetail string\n116|\t// Local carries the majors the local installation offered (empty when\n117|\t// the local generation itself is unknown). Peer carries the peer's\n118|\t// single offered major (zero when the peer offer was unusable).\n119|\tLocal []int\n120|\tPeer  int\n121|\t// Cause is the Go sentinel for errors.Is; it never reaches the wire.\n122|\tCause error\n123|}\n124|\n125|// Error renders the refusal without exposing anything beyond the refusal\n126|// facts. Message text is for humans; automation branches on Code/Reason.\n127|func (refusal *Refusal) Error() string {\n128|\tif refusal == nil {\n129|\t\treturn \"meshneg refusal\"\n130|\t}\n131|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"mesh RPC negotiation refused (%s): %s\", refusal.Reason, refusal.Code)\n132|}\n133|\n134|// Unwrap exposes the cause sentinel for errors.Is.\n135|func (refusal *Refusal) Unwrap() error {\n136|\tif refusal == nil {\n137|\t\treturn nil\n138|\t}\n139|\treturn refusal.Cause\n140|}\n141|\n142|// classExit resolves the pinned exit status for a refusal or exposure code\n143|// under the Structured Error version that introduced it. An unregistered\n144|// code or version fails closed: the caller gets an internal error, never a\n145|// guessed exit.\n146|func classExit(version axerror.Version, code axerror.Code) (int, error) {\n147|\treturn axerror.ExitCodeFor(version, code)\n148|}\n149|\n150|// refuse builds a peer-side refusal (incompatible_protocol, exit 6). It is\n151|// used only when incompatibility is actually known from a decoded hello and\n152|// a known local generation, per Section 11.10.1; unframed input never\n153|// reaches this package.\n154|func refuse(reason RefusalReason, cause error, detail string, local []int, peer int) (*Refusal, error) {\n155|\texit, err := classExit(axerror.Version100, axerror.Code(\"incompatible_protocol\"))\n156|\tif err != nil {\n157|\t\treturn nil, err\n158|\t}\n159|\treturn &Refusal{\n160|\t\tCode:     axerror.Code(\"incompatible_protocol\"),\n161|\t\tExitCode: exit,\n162|\t\tReason:   reason,\n163|\t\tDetail:   detail,\n164|\t\tLocal:    append([]int(nil), local...),\n165|\t\tPeer:     peer,\n166|\t\tCause:    cause,\n167|\t}, nil\n168|}\n169|\n170|// LocalMajors maps the local installation's configuration generation\n171|// (config.Configuration.SchemaVersion) to the exact RPC majors that\n172|// installation offers, in ascending order:\n173|//\n174|//   - 1.0.0 offers 2: the base configuration predates the directory and\n175|//     TerminalBackend extensions, so only the Section 11.2-11.3 core.\n176|//   - 2.0.0 offers 2 and 3: the Section 6.4 directory extension pairs with\n177|//     RPC 3 directory replication, and Section 11.8 requires v2 dual-stack.\n178|//   - 3.0.0 offers 2, 3, and 4: the Section 6.5 TerminalBackend extension\n179|//     pairs with RPC 4 evidence replication, and Section 11.9 requires v3\n180|//     dual-stack with preserved v2 interop.\n181|//   - 4.0.0 offers exactly 5: Section 6.6 requires Host Channel 1 and RPC 5\n182|//     for every peer and states that legacy dual-stack obligations never\n183|//     require a Config-4 endpoint to accept legacy.\n184|//\n185|// Any other generation is refused with the invalid_config class (exit 3):\n186|// Section 6.6 makes unknown configuration a refusal, never legacy\n187|// selection. The result is a fresh slice on every call.\n188|func LocalMajors(configVersion string) ([]int, error) {\n189|\tswitch configVersion {\n190|\tcase \"1.0.0\":\n191|\t\treturn []int{2}, nil\n192|\tcase \"2.0.0\":\n193|\t\treturn []int{2, 3}, nil\n194|\tcase \"3.0.0\":\n195|\t\treturn []int{2, 3, 4}, nil\n196|\tcase \"4.0.0\":\n197|\t\treturn []int{5}, nil\n198|\tdefault:\n199|\t\texit, err := classExit(axerror.Version100, axerror.Code(\"invalid_config\"))\n200|\t\tif err != nil {\n201|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n202|\t\t}\n203|\t\treturn nil, &Refusal{\n204|\t\t\tCode:     axerror.Code(\"invalid_config\"),\n205|\t\t\tExitCode: exit,\n206|\t\t\tReason:   ReasonUnknownConfig,\n207|\t\t\tDetail:   fmt.Sprintf(\"configuration generation %q offers no RPC major\", configVersion),\n208|\t\t\tCause:    ErrUnknownConfig,\n209|\t\t}\n210|\t}\n211|}\n212|\n213|// semverMajor parses a strict semantic version and returns its major\n214|// component. The grammar is the same full semver rpcwire enforces on hello\n215|// contract arrays (major.minor.patch with optional prerelease and build\n216|// metadata, no leading zeros, no \"v\" prefix); agreement with rpcwire decode\n217|// is measured by test, not asserted by comment.\n218|var semverMajor = regexp.MustCompile(`^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(?:-(?:0|[1-9][0-9]*|[0-9]*[A-Za-z-][0-9A-Za-z-]*)(?:\\.(?:0|[1-9][0-9]*|[0-9]*[A-Za-z-][0-9A-Za-z-]*))*)?(?:\\+[0-9A-Za-z-]+(?:\\.[0-9A-Za-z-]+)*)?$`)\n219|\n220|func majorOf(version string) (int, error) {\n221|\tmatch := semverMajor.FindStringSubmatch(version)\n222|\tif match == nil {\n223|\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: version %q is not strict semver\", ErrMixedMajor, version)\n224|\t}\n225|\tmajor, err := strconv.Atoi(match[1])\n226|\tif err != nil {\n227|\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: version %q has no numeric major\", ErrMixedMajor, version)\n228|\t}\n229|\treturn major, nil\n230|}\n231|\n232|// PeerOffer validates the peer's side of the negotiation: the decoded frame\n233|// version plus the decoded hello's contracts map. It returns the peer's\n234|// single offered major. Identity, platform, version, nonce, echo, and limit\n235|// members of the hello are never consulted: negotiation selects a major, it\n236|// does not authenticate, and consulting them here would substitute for the\n237|// admission boundary.\n238|//\n239|// The offer is refused when the frame version is outside the pinned\n240|// vocabulary, when the contracts keys differ from the framing major's exact\n241|// pinned profile (a v2 14-key bound inside a v3+ frame, an extension key, or\n242|// any missing key), when the rpc array is empty or not strictly\n243|// sorted-unique, when any rpc version is not strict semver, or when any rpc\n244|// major differs from the framing major. A v2 frame may carry a 1-16 version\n245|// minor range (Section 11.2); selecting within that range stays a stated\n246|// bound, since this package negotiates majors only.\n247|func PeerOffer(frameVersion string, hello rpcwire.Hello) (int, error) {\n248|\tframing, pinned := pinnedFrameVersions[frameVersion]\n249|\tif !pinned {\n250|\t\trefusal, err := refuse(ReasonUnsupportedFrame, ErrUnsupportedFrame,\n251|\t\t\tfmt.Sprintf(\"frame version %q is outside the pinned 2.0.0-5.0.0 vocabulary\", frameVersion), nil, 0)\n252|\t\tif err != nil {\n253|\t\t\treturn 0, err\n254|\t\t}\n255|\t\treturn 0, refusal\n256|\t}\n257|\tprofile, err := rpcwire.ContractProfile(frameVersion)\n258|\tif err != nil {\n259|\t\treturn 0, err\n260|\t}\n261|\tif len(hello.Contracts) != len(profile) {\n262|\t\treturn 0, shapeRefusal(framing)\n263|\t}\n264|\tfor key := range profile {\n265|\t\tif _, ok := hello.Contracts[key]; !ok {\n266|\t\t\treturn 0, shapeRefusal(framing)\n267|\t\t}\n268|\t}\n269|\toffered := hello.Contracts[\"rpc\"]\n270|\tif len(offered) < 1 || len(offered) > 16 {\n271|\t\treturn 0, shapeRefusal(framing)\n272|\t}\n273|\tfor index, version := range offered {\n274|\t\tmajor, err := majorOf(version)\n275|\t\tif err != nil {\n276|\t\t\treturn 0, mixedRefusal(fmt.Sprintf(\"rpc version %q is not strict semver\", version))\n277|\t\t}\n278|\t\tif major != framing {\n279|\t\t\treturn 0, mixedRefusal(fmt.Sprintf(\"rpc version %q mixes major %d into a major-%d frame\", version, major, framing))\n280|\t\t}\n281|\t\tif index > 0 && offered[index-1] >= version {\n282|\t\t\treturn 0, mixedRefusal(\"rpc versions are not strictly sorted unique\")\n283|\t\t}\n284|\t}\n285|\tif frameVersion != \"2.0.0\" && !slices.Equal(offered, profile[\"rpc\"]) {\n286|\t\treturn 0, shapeRefusal(framing)\n287|\t}\n288|\treturn framing, nil\n289|}\n290|\n291|func shapeRefusal(framing int) error {\n292|\trefusal, err := refuse(ReasonContractShape, ErrContractShape,\n293|\t\tfmt.Sprintf(\"hello contracts do not match the pinned major-%d profile\", framing), nil, 0)\n294|\tif err != nil {\n295|\t\treturn err\n296|\t}\n297|\treturn refusal\n298|}\n299|\n300|func mixedRefusal(detail string) error {\n301|\trefusal, err := refuse(ReasonMixedMajor, ErrMixedMajor, detail, nil, 0)\n302|\tif err != nil {\n303|\t\treturn err\n304|\t}\n305|\treturn refusal\n306|}\n307|\n308|// Select returns the highest major in the intersection of the local and peer\n309|// offer sets. Either set naming a major outside the pinned 2/3/4/5\n310|// vocabulary, an empty set on either side, or a disjoint pair is refused as\n311|// no-common-major: an unmentionable major can never be common, and Section\n312|// 17.1 forbids selecting one by coercion.\n313|func Select(local, peer []int) (int, error) {\n314|\tfor _, major := range local {\n315|\t\tif major < 2 || major > 5 {\n316|\t\t\trefusal, err := refuse(ReasonNoCommonMajor, ErrNoCommonMajor,\n317|\t\t\t\tfmt.Sprintf(\"local offer names major %d outside the pinned 2/3/4/5 vocabulary\", major), append([]int(nil), local...), 0)\n318|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n319|\t\t\t\treturn 0, err\n320|\t\t\t}\n321|\t\t\treturn 0, refusal\n322|\t\t}\n323|\t}\n324|\tfor _, major := range peer {\n325|\t\tif major < 2 || major > 5 {\n326|\t\t\trefusal, err := refuse(ReasonNoCommonMajor, ErrNoCommonMajor,\n327|\t\t\t\tfmt.Sprintf(\"peer offer names major %d outside the pinned 2/3/4/5 vocabulary\", major), append([]int(nil), local...), 0)\n328|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n329|\t\t\t\treturn 0, err\n330|\t\t\t}\n331|\t\t\treturn 0, refusal\n332|\t\t}\n333|\t}\n334|\tbest := 0\n335|\tfor _, candidate := range local {\n336|\t\tif slices.Contains(peer, candidate) && candidate > best {\n337|\t\t\tbest = candidate\n338|\t\t}\n339|\t}\n340|\tif best == 0 {\n341|\t\tpeerMajor := 0\n342|\t\tif len(peer) == 1 {\n343|\t\t\tpeerMajor = peer[0]\n344|\t\t}\n345|\t\trefusal, err := refuse(ReasonNoCommonMajor, ErrNoCommonMajor,\n346|\t\t\t\"local and peer offers share no major (\"+joinMajors(local)+\" against \"+joinMajors(peer)+\")\",\n347|\t\t\tappend([]int(nil), local...), peerMajor)\n348|\t\tif err != nil {\n349|\t\t\treturn 0, err\n350|\t\t}\n351|\t\treturn 0, refusal\n352|\t}\n353|\treturn best, nil\n354|}\n355|\n356|func joinMajors(majors []int) string {\n357|\tparts := make([]string, 0, len(majors))\n358|\tfor _, major := range majors {\n359|\t\tparts = append(parts, strconv.Itoa(major))\n360|\t}\n361|\treturn \"[\" + strings.Join(parts, \" \") + \"]\"\n362|}\n363|\n364|// FeatureActivation reports how one above-core feature is exposed for the\n365|// negotiated peer. It carries no inventory counts, no object IDs, and no\n366|// capability advertisement: Negotiated states the outcome of this selection,\n367|// and Code names the registered exposure code only when the feature was not\n368|// negotiated, so a core-only peer can never be mistaken for an empty one.\n369|type FeatureActivation struct {\n370|\t// Feature is \"directory\" or \"terminal_backend_evidence\".\n371|\tFeature string\n372|\t// Negotiated is true exactly when the selected major carries the\n373|\t// feature (directory at 3+, backend evidence at 4+).\n374|\tNegotiated bool\n375|\t// Code is empty when negotiated; otherwise the registered exposure\n376|\t// code with ExitCode 6.\n377|\tCode     axerror.Code\n378|\tExitCode int\n379|}\n380|\n381|// PeerView is the local node's exposure of the negotiated peer: which\n382|// above-core activations the selection carries and which it reports\n383|// unsupported. Core sync itself is the negotiated major, not a member here.\n384|type PeerView struct {\n385|\tDirectory       FeatureActivation\n386|\tBackendEvidence FeatureActivation\n387|}\n388|\n389|// Decision is the pure-data selection outcome: exactly one common major\n390|// plus the shapes bound to it. Contracts and Namespaces are rebuilt from\n391|// the pinned profile for the selected major, never copied from peer bytes,\n392|// so a malformed peer array cannot propagate past selection.\n393|type Decision struct {\n394|\tMajor           int\n395|\tProtocolVersion string\n396|\tContracts       map[string][]string\n397|\tNamespaces      []string\n398|\tErrorVersion    axerror.Version\n399|\tPeer            PeerView\n400|}\n401|\n402|func exposure(feature string, negotiated bool, code axerror.Code, introduced axerror.Version) (FeatureActivation, error) {\n403|\tactivation := FeatureActivation{Feature: feature, Negotiated: negotiated}\n404|\tif negotiated {\n405|\t\treturn activation, nil\n406|\t}\n407|\texit, err := classExit(introduced, code)\n408|\tif err != nil {\n409|\t\treturn FeatureActivation{}, err\n410|\t}\n411|\tactivation.Code = code\n412|\tactivation.ExitCode = exit\n413|\treturn activation, nil\n414|}\n415|\n416|func decisionFor(major int) (Decision, error) {\n417|\tversion := fmt.Sprintf(\"%d.0.0\", major)\n418|\tcontracts, err := rpcwire.ContractProfile(version)\n419|\tif err != nil {\n420|\t\treturn Decision{}, err\n421|\t}\n422|\tnamespaces, err := rpcwire.Namespaces(version)\n423|\tif err != nil {\n424|\t\treturn Decision{}, err\n425|\t}\n426|\tbound, err := axerror.BindingFor(axerror.ContainingContract{ID: \"urn:ax:protocol:rpc\", Major: major})\n427|\tif err != nil {\n428|\t\treturn Decision{}, err\n429|\t}\n430|\tdirectory, err := exposure(\"directory\", major >= directoryFeatureMajor, DirectoryUnsupportedCode, axerror.Version120)\n431|\tif err != nil {\n432|\t\treturn Decision{}, err\n433|\t}\n434|\tbackend, err := exposure(\"terminal_backend_evidence\", major >= backendEvidenceFeatureMajor, BackendEvidenceUnsupportedCode, axerror.Version130)\n435|\tif err != nil {\n436|\t\treturn Decision{}, err\n437|\t}\n438|\treturn Decision{\n439|\t\tMajor:           major,\n440|\t\tProtocolVersion: version,\n441|\t\tContracts:       contracts,\n442|\t\tNamespaces:      namespaces,\n443|\t\tErrorVersion:    bound,\n444|\t\tPeer:            PeerView{Directory: directory, BackendEvidence: backend},\n445|\t}, nil\n446|}\n447|\n448|// Negotiate selects exactly one common Mesh RPC major for the local\n449|// configuration generation and the peer's decoded hello frame. configVersion\n450|// is the local config.Configuration.SchemaVersion; frameVersion is the\n451|// decoded envelope's protocol_version; hello is the decoded hello body.\n452|//\n453|// On success it returns the Decision for the highest common major. On\n454|// refusal it returns a *Refusal carrying the pinned Section 15 class:\n455|// incompatible_protocol with exit 6 when the decoded inputs prove the\n456|// majors are disjoint or the peer offer is malformed, or invalid_config\n457|// with exit 3 when the local generation is unknown. Any other error is an\n458|// internal registry inconsistency, never a peer verdict.\n459|//\n460|// Negotiate consults only the configuration generation, the frame version,\n461|// and the hello contracts map. It reads no environment, no argv, no raw\n462|// frame bytes, no extension member, and no prior-handshake state, so none\n463|// of those can select a fallback (Section 6.6). It performs no admission:\n464|// the hello identity, allowlist, and trust generation must still pass the\n465|// hostchannel boundary before any dispatch.\n466|func Negotiate(configVersion, frameVersion string, hello rpcwire.Hello) (Decision, error) {\n467|\tlocal, err := LocalMajors(configVersion)\n468|\tif err != nil {\n469|\t\treturn Decision{}, err\n470|\t}\n471|\tpeer, err := PeerOffer(frameVersion, hello)\n472|\tif err != nil {\n473|\t\tif refusal, ok := err.(*Refusal); ok {\n474|\t\t\trefusal.Local = append([]int(nil), local...)\n475|\t\t\treturn Decision{}, refusal\n476|\t\t}\n477|\t\treturn Decision{}, err\n478|\t}\n479|\tmajor, err := Select(local, []int{peer})\n480|\tif err != nil {\n481|\t\treturn Decision{}, err\n482|\t}\n483|\treturn decisionFor(major)\n484|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c479","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b051-fe1f-7003-b3e2-8d6f1f519698"},"sequence":151,"recorded_at":1780531400000297,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0526d3075808030d2006d473e28","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-5-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-219okr) { checklist outcomeResources notes }' 2>&1 | head -n 120\",\n  \"description\": \"Read task checklist and resources\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Negotiate supported majors, preserve core-only peers, expose unsupported directory/backend activation, and refuse no-common-major\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft \\\\u003ccheckpoint_oid\\\\u003e` before completing again.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":true}],\\\"notes\\\":\\\"TASK-260908-2tkufa assigns the approved v0.6.0 delta owner. Original AC and partial work remain preserved; pending runtime support is not claimed by catalog adoption. Own subsequent major negotiation under sections 11.2-11.3/17 with adopted RPC 5 and explicit historical RPC 2/3/4 bounds. Config-4 Host Channel endpoints select RPC 5 only; legacy installations keep explicit historical behavior. Negotiation cannot downgrade a required authenticated endpoint or substitute for TASK-260830-z1yxg9 admission.\\\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/max pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:009eecf230ad676c71fa02f210ad171dc6936cae601b3bc028fa753d219ff3c1 rationale=\\\\\\\"Next fan-out (M2 first leaf: RPC major negotiation over rpcwire/hostchannel) unblocked by STORY-260830-1kiyj6; muse-spark max is the primary configured producer.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260917-b15a5b, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260917-b15a5b)\\\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (muse) (exit=0)\\\\nspawn run completed: muse (run=RUN-260917-b15a5b, pid=76784, exit=0)\\\\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260917-b15a5b queued successor RUN-260917-244f06 (attempt 1/3, model=muse-spark): Change Request construction for TASK-260830-219okr failed: Change Request CR-TASK-260830-219okr-1 revision 1 validation failed at command 5/27 (1-based) with exit code 1; log resource TASK-260830-219okr_change-request_rev1-validation.log; retry: fix the failure and complete the producer again; the configured suite will rerun automatically\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260917-244f06)\\\",\\\"outcomeResources\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260917-b15a5b.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260917-b15a5b.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"System spawn log captured by task-board\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-219okr_results.md\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_results.md\\\",\\\"desc