{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c66f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b051-fe1f-7003-b3e2-8d6f1f519698"},"sequence":402,"recorded_at":1780531400000799,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b053-b7b0-7b72-abeb-3487b4fd1f24"},"task_id":"01a0b053-b7b0-7b72-abeb-3487b4fd1f24","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b053-b7b0-7b72-abeb-3487b4fd1f24","chunk":"Read text file `internal/meshneg/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-219okr clause coverage (package-local)\n2|\n3|Normative authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md` at commit\n4|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6` (relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0).\n5|Historical scope retained: SPEC v0.5.0 (commit `28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`),\n6|Sections 11.2-11.3 and 17. This leaf does not edit `internal/traceability`;\n7|the story's final leaf carries the registry bindings and re-pin.\n8|\n9|## Covered clauses\n10|\n11|| Clause | Rule | Call site | Test |\n12|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n13|| 6.4 | Config-2 directory extension pairs with RPC 3 | LocalMajors (\"2.0.0\" offers 2,3) | TestLocalMajors, TestNegotiateMatrix |\n14|| 6.5 | Config-3 TerminalBackend extension pairs with RPC 4 | LocalMajors (\"3.0.0\" offers 2,3,4) | TestLocalMajors, TestNegotiateMatrix |\n15|| 6.6 | Config-4 requires Host Channel 1 and RPC 5 for every peer | LocalMajors (\"4.0.0\" offers exactly 5) | TestConfig4NeverDowngrades |\n16|| 6.6 | Legacy dual-stack obligations never require Config-4 to accept legacy | Negotiate (Config-4 x legacy refuses) | TestConfig4NeverDowngrades |\n17|| 6.6 | Unknown configuration is a refusal, never legacy selection | LocalMajors default | TestLocalMajors unknown-* |\n18|| 6.6 | No sniffing, extension, argv, env, or failed handshake selects a fallback | Negotiate signature and body | TestNoFallbackSurface |\n19|| 11.2 | 14-key hello contracts; unknown members fail; absent contract is incompatible_protocol | PeerOffer shape checks | TestPeerOfferRefusals/shape, TestSemverAgreementWithRPCWire |\n20|| 11.2 | Unsupported major closes without a peer error frame; initiator emits locally | Refusal (frames nothing) | TestRefusalShape, TestRefusalClassesResolveFromTheRegistry |\n21|| 11.3 | Closed operation registry and envelope discipline | (precondition: caller decodes via rpcwire first) | decodedHello fixtures in every matrix test |\n22|| 11.8 | v3/v2 dual-stack; v2 negotiation is core-only; peer exposed as directory_mesh_unsupported, never zero inventory | decisionFor, PeerView | TestPeerExposure, TestExposureCarriesNoInventory |\n23|| 11.8 | Exact 24-key map and 7 namespaces; v2 bounds invalid in v3 | PeerOffer, decisionFor via rpcwire | TestPeerOfferRefusals, TestDecisionShapes |\n24|| 11.9 | v4 serves v3 dual-stack, preserves v2 interop; backend evidence unsupported rather than empty; both unsupported on v4/v2 | decisionFor, PeerView | TestPeerExposure |\n25|| 11.9 | Exact 25-key map and 8 namespaces; v2/v3 bounds invalid in v4 | PeerOffer, decisionFor via rpcwire | TestPeerOfferRefusals, TestDecisionShapes |\n26|| 11.10.1 | RPC 5 has exact RPC-4 shapes with protocol_version and contracts.rpc 5.0.0; error stays bound to 1.3.0 | decisionFor via rpcwire, axerror | TestDecisionShapes/5.0.0 |\n27|| 11.10.1 | Other RPC majors close without a frame; incompatible_protocol (exit 6) only when actually known | Refusal, Negotiate inputs | TestConfig4NeverDowngrades, TestLegacyNeverSelectsRPC5 |\n28|| 11.10.1 | Hello identity equality, allowlist, and generation are admission, not negotiation | Negotiate (never consulted) | TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission |\n29|| 15.1 | Mesh RPC statically binds per-major error versions; error never a hello key | decisionFor via axerror.BindingFor | TestDecisionShapes |\n30|| 15.1/15.3 | incompatible_protocol exit 6; invalid_config exit 3; directory_mesh_unsupported and terminal_backend_unavailable exit 6 | refuse, exposure via axerror.ExitCodeFor | TestRefusalClassesResolveFromTheRegistry |\n31|| 17.1 | No major selected by coercion; highest mutually supported minor within a common major | PeerOffer mixing refusal, Select | TestPeerOfferRefusals/mixed, TestSelectHighestCommon |\n32|| 17.2 | Reader rejects unsupported major; accepts same/lower minor | pinnedFrameVersions exact match | TestPeerOfferRefusals/frame-versions |\n33|| 17.4 | Report activation unavailable rather than omit the session | BackendEvidenceUnsupportedCode binding | TestPeerExposure |\n34|\n35|## Stated bounds (not covered by this leaf)\n36|\n37|| Bound | Reason |\n38|| --- | --- |\n39|| Within-major minor selection for v2 1-16 ranges | Major negotiation only; any 2.x range selects major 2 (pinned by admitted-ranges) |\n40|| Handshake sequencing (hello-first, request_id echo, one framed refusal then close) | Owned by rpcwire decode plus the connection responder; Negotiate takes decoded hellos |\n41|| Hostchannel admission (identity equality, allowlist, trust generation) | Owned by TASK-260830-z1yxg9; this package proves separation by ignoring those members |\n42|| Fuzzing of rpc operations and version skew | Sibling TASK-260830-19bjfj |\n43|| Registry bindings and digest re-pin in internal/traceability | Story final leaf |\n44|| Crash/idempotency evidence | No durable write exists in this package. Direct imports are errors, fmt, regexp, slices, strconv, strings plus the rpcwire and axerror owners (no os, io, net, time, rand, or exec); the owners are consulted through pure functions only (ContractProfile, Namespaces, ExitCodeFor, BindingFor). Determinism pinned by TestNegotiationIsDeterministic |","final_result":true}}}
