{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c675","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b051-fe1f-7003-b3e2-8d6f1f519698"},"sequence":405,"recorded_at":1780531400000805,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b053-b80d-71f1-8894-b755b7118e95"},"task_id":"01a0b053-b80d-71f1-8894-b755b7118e95","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b053-b80d-71f1-8894-b755b7118e95","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-12-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff LOGBOOK.md README.md 2>&1 | head -n 80; echo ===PATCH-FILES===; grep -E '^\\\\+\\\\+\\\\+ ' '/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_change-request_rev1.patch' 2>&1 | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Review doc diffs and rev1 patch paths\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 43c6d21..c87e6d5 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,13 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-17\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-219okr — dual-stack major negotiation (first leaf)\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/meshneg` (`Negotiate`/`LocalMajors`/`PeerOffer`/`Select` over `Refusal`/`Decision` pure data): generation-to-majors mapping (Config-1: 2; Config-2: 2,3; Config-3: 2,3,4; Config-4: exactly 5), single-major peer-offer validation against the framing major, highest-common selection, no-common-major refusal with registry-resolved `incompatible_protocol`/6 (unknown config: `invalid_config`/3), exact per-major contracts/namespaces/bound error versions rebuilt from rpcwire/axerror, and core-only peer exposure (`directory_mesh_unsupported`, `terminal_backend_unavailable`), never zero inventory. Frames nothing, admits nothing, pure/stateless. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- BINDING CHOICE: the RPC-4 exposure equivalent is the registered `terminal_backend_unavailable` (exit 6), not a minted token — Section 11.9 requires reporting evidence unsupported rather than empty and 17.4 requires reporting activation unavailable; the 1.3.0 exit-6 row carries exactly that code. Refusal/exposure exits resolve via `axerror.ExitCodeFor` under each code's introducing version; cross-version stability is asserted by test, not assumed.\\n+- MUTANTS: 28 narrowing probes killed by named tests (neutral passed, harmless Detail-text control SURVIVED as designed; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`). Two initial SURVIVEDs were test gaps the harness caught: substituted-keys (same count, caught by membership loop, not length check) and peer-mixing-1-beside-common (unobservable without overlap) — both closed with new cases before the evidence run.\\n+- BOUNDS: v2 1-16 minor ranges select the major only (within-major minor selection future work); handshake sequencing stays with rpcwire decode + the responder; admission (identity/allowlist/generation) stays with TASK-260830-z1yxg9 with separation pinned by `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission`; no `ax` command, doctor result, or capability claimed. Traceability registry/digest untouched for the story final leaf (package-local TRACEABILITY.md only).\\n+- AC: 11 of 11 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n - DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n - F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 1f8fc60..b2d71a6 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -3522,9 +3522,25 @@ stream with zero traffic (measured: the product fences the next dispatch and\\n `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; `serveLoop` carries no background\\n watchdog). Section 11.10.5 upstream vectors are source evidence only.\\n \\n+[`internal/meshneg`](internal/meshneg) selects the single Mesh RPC major for\\n+one peer connection from the local configuration generation and the peer's\\n+decoded hello: Config-4 offers exactly RPC 5, legacy generations offer the\\n+historical dual-stack sets, the peer offer must agree with its framing major,\\n+and a disjoint pair refuses no-common-major with `incompatible_protocol`\\n+(exit 6) from actually known inputs. A selection carries the exact pinned\\n+contracts map, namespace vocabulary, and bound Structured Error version for\\n+its major, and reports above-core activation the selection does not carry as\\n+explicitly unsupported (`directory_mesh_unsupported`,\\n+`terminal_backend_unavailable`), never as zero inventory. Outcomes are pure\\n+data: nothing is framed, connected, advertised, or admitted here. There is\\n+no `ax` command, doctor result, or capability claim.\\n+\\n | Tool / check | Exact command | Output |\\n | --- | --- | --- |\\n | RPC/host-channel behavior | `go test ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel -count=1 -v` | stdout; `.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/` logs |\\n+| Major-negotiation behavior | `go test ./internal/meshneg -count=1 -v` | stdout; `.temp/TASK-260830-219okr/` logs |\\n+| Major-negotiation races and coverage | `go test ./internal/meshneg -race -count=1 -cover` | Race diagnostics and measured package coverage |\\n+| Major-negotiation narrowing | `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/meshneg/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-219okr/mutations-meshneg` | 28 narrowing probes killed by named tests plus neutral and harmless SURVIVED controls, in per-plant raw logs and mutant tables; source originals remain untouched |\\n | RPC/host-channel races and coverage | `go test ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel -race -count=1 -cover` | Race diagnostics and measured package coverage |\\n | RPC/host-channel narrowing | `python3 internal/rpcwire/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/mutations-rpcwire` and `python3 internal/hostchannel/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/mutations-hostchannel` | Applied compiling overlays, JSON events, real exits, named failing tests and mutant tables; source originals remain untouched |\\n | Hostile-network conformance | `go test ./internal/hostchannel -run 'TestHostile' -count=1 -v` | Per-vector refusal classes, census assertions, and the OpenSSH loopback lane (skips with an asserted reason when `sshd` cannot bind); `.temp/TASK-260830-2x16gz/` logs |\\n===PATCH-FILES===\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n+++ b/internal/meshneg/README.md\\n+++ b/internal/meshneg/TRACEABILITY.md\\n+++ b/internal/meshneg/conformance_test.go\\n+++ b/internal/meshneg/mutations.py\\n+++ b/internal/meshneg/negotiate.go\\n+++ b/internal/meshneg/negotiate_test.go\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6573,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1644,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
