{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c831","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b051-fe1f-7003-b3e2-8d6f1f519698"},"sequence":627,"recorded_at":1780531400001249,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6cba34f-41b8-4fac-9aa3-0e4eec26db87"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b05f-6231-75b3-8e49-e5b51b3d465c"},"task_id":"01a0b05f-6231-75b3-8e49-e5b51b3d465c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b05f-6231-75b3-8e49-e5b51b3d465c","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-219okr results — implement-dual-stack-major-negotiation\n2|\n3|Role: developer. Status: ready for review (candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree).\n4|\n5|## Deliverable\n6|\n7|`internal/meshneg` (`negotiate.go`, ~470 lines): pure-data major negotiation for Mesh RPC.\n8|\n9|- `LocalMajors(configVersion)` — generation to offered majors: Config-1 → `[2]`,\n10|  Config-2 → `[2 3]`, Config-3 → `[2 3 4]`, Config-4 → exactly `[5]`; unknown\n11|  generations refuse `invalid_config`/exit 3 (Section 6.6: unknown configuration is\n12|  a refusal, never legacy selection).\n13|- `PeerOffer(frameVersion, hello)` — validates the decoded peer frame: pinned\n14|  vocabulary 2.0.0–5.0.0, exact per-major contracts keys (a v2 14-key bound inside a\n15|  v3+ frame refuses), single-major strictly sorted-unique semver rpc array agreeing\n16|  with the framing major. Any mixing refuses `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6.\n17|- `Select(local, peer)` — highest common major; inputs outside 2/3/4/5 or disjoint\n18|  pairs refuse `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6.\n19|- `Negotiate(configVersion, frameVersion, hello)` — production entry returning\n20|  `Decision` (major, protocol version, exact contracts map, namespace vocabulary,\n21|  statically bound Structured Error version, peer exposure) or `*Refusal` (pinned\n22|  Section 15 class + reason + offer facts). Frames nothing: Sections 11.2/15.1/11.10.1\n23|  close without a peer frame on unsupported majors; the initiator maps the class\n24|  to its own local error.\n25|- Core-only preservation: `Decision.Peer` reports directory activation as\n26|  `directory_mesh_unsupported` and backend-evidence activation as\n27|  `terminal_backend_unavailable` (registered exit-6 codes; exits resolved via\n28|  `axerror.ExitCodeFor`), never as zero inventory. No count/inventory member exists\n29|  in the view (structurally pinned by test).\n30|\n31|## AC coverage: 11 of 11 rows driven\n32|\n33|See `TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md` for the row-by-row call sites and\n34|named tests. Every refusal gate has negative tests plus at least one narrowing mutant.\n35|\n36|## Files changed (UNCOMMITTED, Story worktree only)\n37|\n38|- `internal/meshneg/negotiate.go` (new, production)\n39|- `internal/meshneg/negotiate_test.go`, `internal/meshneg/conformance_test.go` (new, tests)\n40|- `internal/meshneg/mutations.py` (new, shipped mutant harness)\n41|- `internal/meshneg/README.md`, `internal/meshneg/TRACEABILITY.md` (new, docs)\n42|- `README.md` (Mesh RPC section: paragraph + 3 tool rows; measured-coverage\n43|  subsection untouched), `LOGBOOK.md` (newest-first entry)\n44|- `internal/traceability` untouched (final leaf owns registry bindings + re-pin)\n45|\n46|## Test evidence (all exits real, logs in the evidence tar)\n47|\n48|- `go test ./internal/meshneg -count=1 -v` → ok, 15/15 tests pass\n49|- `go test ./internal/meshneg -race -count=1 -cover` → ok, 87.8% statements\n50|- Mutants: `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/meshneg/mutations.py\n51|  --output .temp/TASK-260830-219okr/mutations-meshneg` → exit 0; 28 narrowing\n52|  probes killed by named tests, neutral passed, harmless `detail-text` control\n53|  survived as designed; per-plant raw logs + exits + table archived; no `__pycache__`\n54|- Full configured validation suite (commands 0–26): all green —\n55|  gofmt, build, vet, `go test ./...` verbose (38 ok / 0 FAIL), race (38 ok),\n56|  cover (38 lines), 14 fuzz smokes, tracecheck, cataloggen `-adopted -check`,\n57|  linux + windows builds, JSON census, `task-board validate` (exit 0),\n58|  `git diff --check`\n59|\n60|## Binding choices and bounds\n61|\n62|- RPC-4 exposure equivalent is the registered `terminal_backend_unavailable`\n63|  (exit 6): Section 11.9 requires reporting evidence unsupported rather than empty,\n64|  Section 17.4 requires reporting activation unavailable, and the 1.3.0 exit-6 row\n65|  carries exactly that code. No code minted.\n66|- Refusal/exposure exits resolve under each code's introducing Error version\n67|  (1.0.0/1.2.0/1.3.0); cross-version exit stability is asserted by test.\n68|- v2 1–16 rpc minor ranges select the major only; within-major minor selection is\n69|  future work (pinned by `admitted-ranges`).\n70|- Handshake sequencing (hello-first, request_id echo, one framed refusal then close)\n71|  stays with rpcwire decode + the connection responder; admission stays with\n72|  TASK-260830-z1yxg9 (separation pinned by `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission`).\n73|- No durable writes: direct imports exclude os/io/net/time/rand/exec; owners\n74|  consulted through pure functions only; statelessness pinned by\n75|  `TestNegotiationIsDeterministic`. No crash/idempotency surface.\n76|- No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is claimed.","final_result":true}}}
